{
  // Type-checks `scripts/` ONLY, and emits nothing.
  //
  // History: `scripts/` was first kept out of `tsconfig.json` because that
  // config used to EMIT `dist/` with `rootDir: "src"`, and adding `scripts`
  // would have moved the output to `dist/src/…`. Since 2026-11-13 nothing in
  // this package emits with `tsc`: `tsconfig.json` sets `noEmit`, and
  // `scripts/build.mjs` bundles `dist/index.js` with esbuild. The two configs
  // stay separate for the reason below.
  //
  // It includes `scripts` and NOT `src`, so the two passes do not overlap:
  // `tsc --noEmit` checks the files under `src`, this checks the `.ts` files
  // under `scripts`, and nothing is checked twice. (`scripts/build.mjs` and
  // `scripts/check-start.mjs` are plain JavaScript, so this pass does not
  // check them: `allowJs` is off.) That is only safe because
  // `scripts/` imports nothing from `src` — today only `@prisma/client`,
  // `vitest`, node builtins and its own sibling modules. **If a script ever
  // imports from `src`, TypeScript will pull those files into this program and
  // check them again here.** That is correct but no longer free, so check what
  // it costs before adding such an import.
  //
  // This pass covers test files too. That is why
  // `scripts/databaseIsolation.test.ts` is type-checked. It costs about 0.5s of
  // server build time, because importing `vitest` adds 46 declaration files —
  // see the root CLAUDE.md for the measured before/after.
  //
  // `apps/web` gained its own test pass on 2026-10-30 (issue #340,
  // `apps/web/tsconfig.test.json`). This comment used to say `apps/web`'s pass
  // did not cover test files, which was true until that day and is now wrong.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "rootDir": ".",
    "noEmit": true
  },
  "include": ["scripts"],
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist"]
}
